{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book","id":32023,"title":"Am I the only RPG Nerd that never read a DnD book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-17T17:36:03-08:00","id":32023,"title":"Am I the only RPG Nerd that never read a DnD book?","content":"Seriously, I got started on Werewolf Revised... and most of my experience has been with Whitewolf, I have a few other RPGs but I don't have DnD books... I know some day I need to read at least one but... am I alone in this? It seems virtually everyone else I know who I haven't introduced into roleplaying started with DnD or is most comfortable with DnD?<br /> <br /> I mean I got to play very briefly one Summer when I was visiting my Exalted Group and they played DnD since the only people comfortable enough with a system to run a game were from the DnD end of things. But I use mostly WW terminology preferring the Term ST to Dungeon Master, with Game Master as an acceptable Middle Ground, and Hollyhock God as a catchy alternate.<br /> <br /> But when asking about how DnD works from my friends that specialized in it... they didn't seem know as much as beyond what feats do and classes. For instance it took me forever to hammer out that DnD is just a rules set but what it isn't really a setting right? I mean it will give you cultures and gods but you have to go to things like Forgotten Realms or Pathfinder for actual Worlds? So basic DnD just forces the GM to make a world, which some love and some don't.<br /> <br /> I mean I absorbed DnD knowledge basically from reverse engineering concepts from Video Games Stolen from it.<br /> <br /> When introducing DnD Players to Whitewolf games they seem to hemorrhage their brains when I explain to them how Whitewolf handles Exp, and that you don't just choose a Race and add a class. Like seriously I tried getting someone who just showed up for one game of Exalted, was a friend of two of the Players, and she wanted to play an Elf Mage and I had to explain that isn't what you would think it is in Exalted, and how Exalted are more then just some common profession, how Elf can mean a number of things, and how the magic of DnD and Exalted were kind of different.<br /> <br /> On the good side some of the previously only DnD Players loved the fact that Whitewolf games was about more then Dungeon Crawling and how they could be jungle Rockstar Goddesses, or Russian Gypsy Demigods. They loved the interaction, and the fact that the setting was built around NPCs important to their characters history.<br /> <br /> So am I alone, or are their other Freaks that are alien to DnD?<br /> <br /> Also... I never really got into Magic the Gathering...so uhh please don't confiscate my Nerd Badge... I had to hurt an awful lot of fellows to get it... :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T17:39:33-08:00","id":32026,"title":"","content":"I've have also never read a DnD book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T18:19:51-08:00","id":32051,"title":"","content":"I started with D&amp;D, but that's mostly because it's the most common game. It's the gateway drug into the industry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T19:19:30-08:00","id":32082,"title":"","content":"Yes, D&amp;D is a set of rules used to play fantasy adventure. However, each edition has balanced itself between being just a rules set, and presenting itself with a setting which DMs could use if they wanted to. 3E has Greyhawk mixed in the core books. 4E started with the Points of Light, which evolved into the Nentir Vale setting. WOTC has announced 5E will be packaged with Forgotten Realms to start with. Nothing in the books insisted you use those settings, and they gave you all the tools to build your own. So your initial impression that it was both a rules set and a setting was not really all that far off.<br /> <br /> Technically, Pathfinder is also just a rules set and Golarion is the setting. Much like D&amp;D, Pathfinder works for any number of published or homebrew settings.<br /> <br /> If you want to check out D&amp;D, go for it, but don't feel like you need to. D&amp;D was the only game in town for a minute, but we are long past the time when it defined this hobby. I meet more and more people every year who have never played it, and that is fine. It just shows us how far we have grown beyond our roots.<br /> <br /> As for your Nerd Badge... Well, we need to hold a committee meeting, and we will get back to you on that.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T19:27:51-08:00","id":32091,"title":"","content":"I want to see a 5th ed Ravenloft setting, that would get me to buy a new DnD product after not buying anything since about 2002.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T20:32:02-08:00","id":32122,"title":"","content":"Gateway drug indeed. Never played any RPG. But I did love poring through the books. Way back when I first began going through them, it was near that dawn of time, the 70s. Gary Gygax had began Dragon Magazine a couple of years earlier. *sigh* Still have Deities and Demigods...(Newhon Mythos, and Melnibone Mythos in it) ... o the memories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T20:47:15-08:00","id":32132,"title":"","content":"I don't know if you can call yourself an RPG nerd if you've never read a D&amp;D book. It would be like calling yourself a science fiction TV show nerd without having seen Star Trek or a Fantasy Novel nerd without having read Tolkien. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I started with D&amp;D back in the late 80's. Though since then I've played almost every RPG system under the sun. And the thing I've discovered is that the system is ultimately kind of meaningless. It's just a framework to let you tell stories and, while some systems let you tell certain types of stories a little bit easier, ultimately you can tell any type of story using any type of system.<br /> <br /> Honestly though it probably wouldn't be a bad idea to check out a D&amp;D book or two. It might make explaining the similarities and differences between D&amp;D and other systems (like Exalted) a bit easier. Because while there are differences, there's also quite a few basic similarities. Being able to help translate concepts from the new system into a system the players are more familiar with can help them get the hang of things a bit quicker.<br /> <br /> AnubisXy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 12-18-2013, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T22:05:59-08:00","id":32163,"title":"","content":"You're not alone, although I have had a brief brush with D&amp;D. My RPG experiences began with a Vampire: the Masquerade LARP, and have largely consisted of various WW games. I did play in a short-lived D&amp;D 3.5 campaign around 10 years ago, though I'd already been at WW stuff for a long time by then. That's it.<br /> <br /> I don't much care for the d20 System, and generally find D&amp;D to be crunchier than I enjoy.<br /> <br /> Occasional games of Dungeon World, however, are quite fun. It's the same spirit of classic fantasy adventure, but with a far lighter, simpler set of rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\"><b>Demon Cat</b></span><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://flamingporcupine.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Illuminated Dark Ages character sheets and more</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10-demon-cat","name":"Demon Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"266"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T07:03:20-08:00","id":32361,"title":"","content":"I played one session of D&amp;D, never read the book, just got guided thru character creation. Died in 20 minutes. Walked away, never looked back or played again.<br /> <br /> Played some TSR Marvel Super Heroes after that.<br /> <br /> Then someone dragged me to a Masquerade LARP in 1995.<br /> <br /> I've got a few other game companies' books on my shelves, but they are mostly for story ideas for White Wolf games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T08:02:00-08:00","id":32409,"title":"","content":"Never read or played anything D&amp;D, and, frankly, the more I learn about it, the less I think I'd enjoy it.<br /> So...<br /> *timidly raises hand*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T09:09:56-08:00","id":32452,"title":"","content":"I would guess it depends somewhat on how olde you are. The original D&amp;D Red Box was my first rpg, and there weren't a lot of other options. Last I played it was AD&amp;D 2nd edition, but if not for that box I might never have moved on to Rifts, Shadowrun, VTM etc. By the way, I miss the boxed sets from back in the day. It kept your books, maps, sheets, pencils and dice all in one place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T09:44:16-08:00","id":32487,"title":"","content":"Speaking of boxed sets, it isn't D&amp;D but I was there when this came out:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_Realm\" target=\"_blank\"><img src=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_iBDQOXCHTEU/S7D7J1EN4KI/AAAAAAAAAlU/N0VTaIkfbBE/s320/mrbox.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T12:52:27-08:00","id":32651,"title":"","content":"Yep, backwards knowledge from Video Game RPGs (Final Fantasy) too. There were also D&amp;D beat'em up games in arcades too.<br /> I do have one Monster Manual, an adventure with Gnolls on the cover, and a Slayer's Guide to Gnolls D20 book, and one novel that has a Gnoll character in it. Then I would buy Dragon Magazine for some of the mythology articles. I also have two Knights of the Dinner Table comic books. But yeah, I got into White Wolf first thanks to the Rage CCG.<br /> <br /> Pretty much my main interest into D&amp;D was for the Gnolls. That I still think need to be massively re-written or at least have different options of presenting them in game. Because it's so inaccurate to how hyenas really operate. And how I think they would operate if they became humanoid. Then again, D&amp;D was probably written before Jane Goodall's book Innocent Killers or was ignoring Jane's work when the book came out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T13:58:06-08:00","id":32697,"title":"","content":"If I want a gaming console, it will have to be able to play Gauntlet (any game in the line). I had a Xbox and play Dark Legacy to death, then I discover the cheat codes and got to play different characters (favorites were the Japanese schoolgirl and the BDSM midget).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T14:29:39-08:00","id":32715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JadedTrueBrujah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=32697#post32697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I want a gaming console, it will have to be able to play Gauntlet (any game in the line). I had a Xbox and play Dark Legacy to death, then I discover the cheat codes and got to play different characters (favorites were the Japanese schoolgirl and the BDSM midget).</div> </div> </div> </div>JTB, did you mean for this post to go in a different thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T15:10:40-08:00","id":32744,"title":"","content":"Back on track, I'm of the opinion that anyone who plays tabletop RPG's need to play DnD at least once-not necessarily because it's a gold standard, must play game, but because it's important to understand the roots of the activity through experience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T15:15:29-08:00","id":32747,"title":"","content":"I played <b>D&amp;D</b> more than a decade after starting on RPGs, and it bore out my opinion that it was not what I wanted in gaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T15:26:06-08:00","id":32759,"title":"","content":"Someone mentioned Final Fantasy as a possible RPG and Goddess knows I defeated that game when I was pregnant with Elisabeth. Most people don't realize that these games were early forefathers to todays MMORPGs. I even got Oblivion for the PC from my daughter while she has Skyrim for the PS3. I view the industry as the same thing, no matter if it is Bloodlines or Requiem or V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Bipolar vampire...can't decide to feast for fun or for rage...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/101-jadedtruebrujah","name":"JadedTrueBrujah","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T16:23:30-08:00","id":32805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=32744#post32744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on track, I'm of the opinion that anyone who plays tabletop RPG's need to play DnD at least once-not necessarily because it's a gold standard, must play game, but because it's important to understand the roots of the activity through experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say playing it is necessary, although I think knowing your roots is important.<br /> <br /> In Gygax Magazine, issue #1, there is a fantastic article titled 'The cosmology of role-playing games,' by James Carpio. The article is perfect for educating oneself about the history and growth of our hobby. Before I read this article, I had no idea how far we had really come since D&amp;D. I had no idea how much more space there was to grow into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":8,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","user":"Storyteller","date":". 12-18-2013, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-18T18:13:50-08:00","id":32880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=32744#post32744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back on track, I'm of the opinion that anyone who plays tabletop RPG's need to play DnD at least once-not necessarily because it's a gold standard, must play game, but because it's important to understand the roots of the activity through experience.</div> </div> </div> </div>The current D&amp;D is so different from what it was back then, I don't know if I would consider playing it to be actually experiencing the roots of the hobby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":868,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","user":"danelsan","date":". 12-18-2013, 09:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T06:39:11-08:00","id":33136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JadedTrueBrujah</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=32759#post32759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Someone mentioned Final Fantasy as a possible RPG and Goddess knows I defeated that game when I was pregnant with Elisabeth. Most people don't realize that these games were early forefathers to todays MMORPGs. I even got Oblivion for the PC from my daughter while she has Skyrim for the PS3. I view the industry as the same thing, no matter if it is Bloodlines or Requiem or V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha. MU*s were the early forefathers of today's MMORPGs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T09:40:47-08:00","id":33267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=32880#post32880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The current D&amp;D is so different from what it was back then, I don't know if I would consider playing it to be actually experiencing the roots of the hobby.</div> </div> </div> </div>I picked up the new Red Box for nostalgia, not knowing it was the new rules (I thought it might be a reissue of the one I started on). To me it didn't feel like D&amp;D. I called it BattleTech with mages. Not raining on anyone who likes it, gods know the olde system had faults (coughTHAC0cough) but it is completely different. (though I kinda like Tieflings)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T09:49:24-08:00","id":33271,"title":"","content":"I played enough D&amp;D to know that I don't like it very much. I got my start with Shadowrun, though (so, D&amp;D with guns, cyborgs, and laughable representations of hacking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T11:04:21-08:00","id":33310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Am I the only RPG Nerd that never read a DnD book?<br /> </div> </div> </div>no........","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/170-lunatyk","name":"Lunatyk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T12:28:36-08:00","id":33338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=32132#post32132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if you can call yourself an RPG nerd if you've never read a D&amp;D book. It would be like calling yourself a science fiction TV show nerd without having seen Star Trek or a Fantasy Novel nerd without having read Tolkien. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I started with D&amp;D back in the late 80's. Though since then I've played almost every RPG system under the sun. And the thing I've discovered is that the system is ultimately kind of meaningless. It's just a framework to let you tell stories and, while some systems let you tell certain types of stories a little bit easier, ultimately you can tell any type of story using any type of system.<br /> <br /> Honestly though it probably wouldn't be a bad idea to check out a D&amp;D book or two. It might make explaining the similarities and differences between D&amp;D and other systems (like Exalted) a bit easier. Because while there are differences, there's also quite a few basic similarities. Being able to help translate concepts from the new system into a system the players are more familiar with can help them get the hang of things a bit quicker.<br /> <br /> AnubisXy</div> </div> </div> </div>I wonder if it makes me a super nerd for having watched TOS, Next generation and DS9-episodes and all the films multiple times and read every last thing in print that either Christopher Tolkien or his father have written. I've also seen every film and series made from Lotr and The Hobbit. I never quite got sold into MTG though I tried a couple of tournaments at Cons before deciding that Magic wasn't really the game where I'd ever really exalt since I suck at chess too...<br /> <br /> And I had my gate drug by Xeroxing my friends red box D&amp;D back in the 80's from which I gradually slid into more serious stuff such as Role master and Runequest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T15:41:49-08:00","id":35172,"title":"","content":"I've read several, but I think I started with L5R or Scion.<br /> <br /> As for inflexible fans of D&amp;D, Elda I know guys who refuse to play any game that's not a particular Edition of Dungeons and Dragons (3.5, always 3.5), much less an RPG unrelated to it. It's halfway between hilarious and fucking depressing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T22:52:29-08:00","id":35392,"title":"","content":"Yeah I am learning the Hardway that people take it very seriously if they can't have their Orcs/Elves/Dwarves in ALL games... RPG isn't just re-enacting a battle written version of Lord of the Rings, its making characters that you want to play as. Okay World of Warcraft has Orcs... but you can't play an Orc, or a Dwarf in Werewolf... in Werewolf you play a Werewolf...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T12:01:31-08:00","id":35711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Seriously, I got started on Werewolf Revised... and most of my experience has been with Whitewolf, I have a few other RPGs but I don't have DnD books... I know some day I need to read at least one but... am I alone in this? It seems virtually everyone else I know who I haven't introduced into roleplaying started with DnD or is most comfortable with DnD? </div> </div> </div>I started in Vampire: the Masquerade 2nd edition and didn't get near D&amp;D for several years, so I remember feeling like you do now. It seemed like everyone had started in D&amp;D and knew about it, and I had to hear about things like THAC0 without knowing what the hell they were talking about. I didn't think that I'd enjoy the game based on what I heard and I didn't have the money to experiment with at the time, so I shined them on.<br /> <br /> You can shine them on, too, if it suits you. There is no rule which says that you must read, like, or play any version of D&amp;D in order to consider yourself a gamer. Some folks might argue otherwise and might enjoy the feeling of geek cred, but there's no good reason to divide up an already limited audience of a niche hobby for bragging rights. If the games that you play now do it for you, awesome! Rock them! But many tabletop gamers will expect at least a passing familiarity with some of the basics and you will miss out on aspects of conversations if you don't have it. Given its history and influence, it can be difficult to ignore. That said, not everyone needs or wants to explore the roots of the hobby, and you can simply explain that you have other priorities.<br /> <br /> There <b>are</b> solid reasons to give other systems a try, however, whether or not they're D&amp;D, and if only at a con or a game store. The first is that learning different systems will help you understand game mechanics, system strengths and weaknesses, and your own preferences better. It's kind of like learning a second language and understanding language in general in a more nuanced way, and you've already seen it at work when you were teaching D&amp;D players about Exalted.<br /> <br /> Just reading a game book only goes so far, as well; you really need to see how it plays with a well-functioning group in order to see the array of options and the type of experience that game offers. You might find bits and pieces you can port into your own games and vice versa, and which enhance your experience of all games. For instance: I always played D&amp;D with lots of grit and moral gray area, as well as very dark shadows. That is what I brought with me from cWoD. Then I took the joy of charts and tables and such from D&amp;D back to my WoD games.<br /> <br /> And with exposure and actual play - and most importantly, with a fair and open mind - you might discover something you like and/or something that helps give you a welcome break from the types of games you're used to. I found that after some years I needed a break from the WoD (and I was as shocked to get to that point as anybody) and D&amp;D gave me the experience I was craving. If you're lucky, you'll find something you really love and you'll be able to carry it with you. I've moved between D&amp;D and WoD pretty much ever since, and I love them both.<br /> <br /> In the end, you don't have to play multiple systems, you don't have to play them regularly, and you don't have to do anything you don't want to do with your own leisure time. But if you do find another game you like, that'll mean even more fun for you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":227,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","user":"KismetRose","date":". 12-23-2013, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T16:43:26-08:00","id":36626,"title":"","content":"I started with GURPS, and it's still my favorite.<br /> <br /> On topic: I'll play D&amp;D, but not 4e, it's an abomination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1800-randaconda","name":"Randaconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T17:21:26-08:00","id":36637,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I hear a lot of negative stuff about 4e. DnD Next is supposed to return the system back a bit..away from a lot of 4e stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T17:43:35-08:00","id":36648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Randaconda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=36626#post36626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started with GURPS, and it's still my favorite.<br /> <br /> On topic: I'll play D&amp;D, but not 4e, it's an abomination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'd say its not quite an abomination as its a system which mechanically works quite well but its exceedingly rigid -rigid to the point of stifling and boring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T18:18:16-08:00","id":36658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=36648#post36648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I'd say its not quite an abomination as its a system which mechanically works quite well but its exceedingly rigid -rigid to the point of stifling and boring.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's like play WoW, dude. It sucks ass. They took all the good shit from the earlier editions and fucked them up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1800-randaconda","name":"Randaconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T23:52:28-08:00","id":36800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=36637#post36637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I hear a lot of negative stuff about 4e. DnD Next is supposed to return the system back a bit..away from a lot of 4e stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most, If not all of it is bullshit from an echo chamber that refuses to believe people could ever want to buy an edition that wasn't the one they cut their teeth on.<br /> <br /> *looks up*<br /> <br /> Case in point! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for Next, that edition is said to be more like 2nd Edition with Feats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T00:01:10-08:00","id":36804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Randaconda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=36658#post36658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's like play WoW, dude. It sucks ass. They took all the good shit from the earlier editions and fucked them up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes. All the good shit like System Bloat, utterly redundant skills, feat taxes, arbitrary alignment restrictions, CoDzilla, various Classes being straight up <i>worthless</i> and rules and tables for everything, whether it needed it or not.<br /> <br /> I've played and had fun playing 3.5, but honestly that was in spite of the system, not because of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T00:46:43-08:00","id":36810,"title":"","content":"4th edition was a decent system, but it felt incredibly watered down and generic. It got the job done, but it wasn't very interesting or memorable, nor did it feel like a good reflection of the game world. <br /> <br /> AnubisXy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T01:40:21-08:00","id":36817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=36804#post36804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yes. All the good shit like System Bloat, utterly redundant skills, feat taxes, arbitrary alignment restrictions, CoDzilla, various Classes being straight up <i>worthless</i> and rules and tables for everything, whether it needed it or not.<br /> <br /> I've played and had fun playing 3.5, but honestly that was in spite of the system, not because of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So? At least it was a rpg, and not a miniatures game. 4e is only slightly better than FATAL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1800-randaconda","name":"Randaconda","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","v