eonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T14:56:55-08:00","id":37034,"title":"","content":"Wait what? Did I miss something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T23:00:45-08:00","id":37183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Randaconda</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=36817#post36817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4e is only slightly better than FATAL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is unfortunate for 3.5, as it is quite a bit worse than FATAL.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But we should probably stop this before the mods put us on a month long vacation from the site.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-25T23:43:18-08:00","id":37199,"title":"","content":"Started on D&amp;D 3.5, got into Vampire, got into non-Vampire WW games, got into a wide variety of games since then.<br /> <br /> Don't particularly care for D&amp;D nowadays, but only because that's the only thing that gets played and I'm a man who likes his variety. I preferred 4e to 3.X (including Pathfinder) but after 5 hour combats every other week for a few months I'd say I'm also solidly burned out on that game as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T12:13:51-08:00","id":37953,"title":"","content":"I don't like it when people say things like &quot;you can't really call yourself an RPG nerd if you haven't played D&amp;D.&quot;<br /> <br /> That's like trying to tell me that I wasn't a complete fang-geek (vampire buff, or whatever else you might call someone totally into just about everything blood-sucker) until I finally heard about for the first time and played Vampire: the Masquerade in 2001 - a singular niche experience does not define my fandom anywhere near as well as the dozens of myths, hundreds of novels, and thousands of movies I'd absorbed into my life by that point.<br /> <br /> Hell, I was playing D&amp;D for like 7 years, using vampires as villains, mentors, and my own characters on the rare occasion a DM would let me before I was even aware that there was such a company as White Wolf and that they were a full decade into producing a role-playing game specifically about vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T22:29:05-08:00","id":38594,"title":"","content":"People can get pretty goddamned retarded about things like that.<br /> I remember hearing one reviewer inform the audience that you were not a real gamer if you didn't know about <i>Galaga.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T12:34:17-08:00","id":38824,"title":"","content":"Tell me about it. Anime Nation forums was notorious for that kind of thing back in the day. Especially the Final Fantasy section of the forums. You had to deal with obnoxious FF6 fans who had to butt in every conversation thread about FF7 and harass you for daring to talk about it. And I've had those same obnoxious &quot;FF6&quot; fans tell me I wasn't a <b>real</b> FF/JRPG fan because I started out on FF7 and ignored that I stated remembering Dragon Quest and Phantasy Star II as a kid.<br /> <br /> Then again, they never seemed to get in that all their talk about how over-hyped FF7 was, they didn't notice they were over-hyping their own beloved game itself.<br /> I still think the main reason they hated FF7 was because it introduced so many new people into their niche hobby and that FF7 did financially better than FF6 ever did.<br /> Because so many, <i>&quot;You're not a real fan of X because of Y</i>&quot;, always comes off as slightly xenophobic to me.<br /> They also didn't notice that some people didn't just stick to FF7 only, we became interested in video game RPGs because of it and sought out other games in the genre.<br /> <br /> I think what any community/fandom/hobby should not do is drive away any and all newcomers. Because then the community never grows as a result, it stays as a small group and eventually dies off because of it.<br /> <br /> And yeah, I know that not all FF6 or old school FF fans are like this. But usually the big warning bell for me, is when they start ranting about FF7 or FF12 for no reason.<br /> If you like RPGs, then you're a RPG nerd. It doesn't matter which RPG you favor to qualify. The same should be said of everything (<i>TV shows, Anime, Cartoons, Comics, RPGs, Video Games, mass etc.</i>).<br /> <br /> I think what's worse is the, <i>&quot;You're not a fan of X because you're a <b>GIRL</b>.&quot;</i>, that's been going on in the comics fandom of late (<i>And has even infected some in the industry itself</i>). I hate it because I was one of those girls that grew up on video games and hot wheels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T12:40:14-08:00","id":38827,"title":"","content":"Never played a game of D&amp;D but I would ( and still do ) read a lot of the books for some writing ideas. I couldn't get a group that was interested in teaching a newbie or wanted to give me a fair try at the game ( me asking a lot during character creation and trying to understand the rules doesn't mean I'm stupid, damn it.... ) before deciding to replace me with someone else.<br /> <br /> Haven't had any luck in any game settings, actually. I did join a LARP with a small group of friends on year at a friend's house and that was pretty fun. I've played a few rounds of Munchkin as well and enjoyed it...other than all my friends that kept using those damn sex change cards on me.... &gt;.&lt; <br /> <br /> I mainly stick to forum role playing that will use some ideas from the different settings. So Eldagusto, if you think you may get your geek cred questioned, what would that make me?<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter what some folks may think of you and what you are able to get into. No &quot;group&quot; of any kind of interest is going to be exactly the same and still count themselves in that group so don't worry about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i><span style=\"color:darkred\">Got an angel on the left hand and a devil on the right<br /> She's gonna raise a little hell up in heaven tonight---Vixen</span></i></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:olive\"><i>When you say it's all divine and meant to be<br /> What about your flesh and blood and defiers like me?---Avantasia</i></span></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/821-rayvin-miyu","name":"Rayvin Miyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T16:23:30-08:00","id":38944,"title":"","content":"Well I figure when I do pick up a DnD book it would probably be whatever current edition first. Like what are they on now 5th?<br /> <br /> <br /> And I got started with Final Fantasy 8... so if you think the FF6 fans rag on FF7 fans you should see how FF8 fans get treated! But the first Video Game RPG I started on was Mario RPG, and that is a legit game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T17:53:12-08:00","id":38992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=38944#post38944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well I figure when I do pick up a DnD book it would probably be whatever current edition first. Like what are they on now 5th?<br /> <br /> <br /> And I got started with Final Fantasy 8... so if you think the FF6 fans rag on FF7 fans you should see how FF8 fans get treated! But the first Video Game RPG I started on was Mario RPG, and that is a legit game!</div> </div> </div> </div>5th is due out this summer.<br /> <br /> There's a large percentage of the followers that just switched over Pathfinder instead of 4th... it's sort of a 3.75 with some solid balancing.<br /> <br /> They've all got ups and downs as systems and things I recommend them for and things I don't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T10:27:02-08:00","id":39474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=38944#post38944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I got started with Final Fantasy 8... so if you think the FF6 fans rag on FF7 fans you should see how FF8 fans get treated! But the first Video Game RPG I started on was Mario RPG, and that is a legit game!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I know (<i>Again, Anime Nation Forums</i>). At the time for me, it took a longer time to get to FF8, as FF Tactics and Suikoden II were what me and my younger sister were playing at the time. When we did get to FF8, I didn't really care for it or like it. But even if I didn't like it, if someone else did, that was fine with me.<br /> <br /> But go to Anime Nation Forums around the early-mid 2000's and FF8 fans had it the worse. Next in line were the FF10 fans (<i>I didn't like the story or characters, but the gameplay was fun. I would usually help out with questions</i> <i>on how to get past a certain thing.</i>). FF9 fans, they didn't go after. They would praise it because it let you have four characters and because it referenced the much older games.<br /> I think what my favorite threads in that section was always what the next game in the series would be. Because all the old school FF fans would flood it saying how they thought the next game would be horrible, but you somehow knew they would be buying it anyways.<br /> <br /> But yeah, the newest game they love to hate is FF12 because it was so MMO-like. I think some people don't get that Spoony is mocking the mindset fanatic older FF fans have on FF12 when he quickly went over it (<i>Because I knew from vlogs, he said he didn't mind it that much</i>).<br /> I do understand why people don't like FF13, and that even non-FF fans wouldn't like it either. I know I'm still considering it as a joke gift for my younger sister, though.<br /> <br /> <u>On-Topic:</u><br /> I think they are working on <b>D&amp;D Next</b>. But anything that lets me play as a Gnoll or has a lot of Gnoll info, I won't mind picking up.<br /> As anyone done what that one Dragon Magazine issue did? Put D&amp;D in a modern, steampunk/victorian, or futuristic setting instead of a basic fantasy one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Rage CCG Collector and Artist. Visit the <a href=\"http://rageccg.proboards.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Rage CCG Forums</a>.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img818/5825/w20supportercliath125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img839/9002/ylxu.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1137-laughing-hyena","name":"Laughing Hyena","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T23:17:00-08:00","id":39821,"title":"","content":"I actually felt like FF12 had the smoothest gameplay and felt the least grindy because it was in real time. :P D&amp;D Next, is that a different setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T04:33:53-08:00","id":39907,"title":"","content":"I beliebe they want to set Next in the Forgotten Realms, at least that's the last thing I heard about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T06:31:52-08:00","id":39938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=39907#post39907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I beliebe they want to set Next in the Forgotten Realms, at least that's the last thing I heard about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the focus is on <a href=\"http://forgottenrealms.wikia.com/wiki/The_Sundering_(series)\" target=\"_blank\">the Sundering</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T16:44:32-08:00","id":40217,"title":"","content":"They aren't actually certain to be treating the Forgotten Realms as the default setting, it is just the first on their priority list of settings to release because it is (historically at least) the most popular campaign setting.<br /> <br /> The original intent was to make the core books ready for any setting by mentioning things like which deities from which real world pantheons and which campaign settings have a particular cleric domain.... there was a poll a bit back about this, but I can't seem to find the results right now to see whether it was the core books being &quot;setting free&quot; or assuming a particular default but acknowledging other possibilities that won out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-31T22:24:09-08:00","id":40357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=39938#post39938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, the focus is on <a href=\"http://forgottenrealms.wikia.com/wiki/The_Sundering_(series)\" target=\"_blank\">the Sundering</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>We'll see how that goes. <br /> <br /> They really shot themselves in the foot with the Spellplague. The Forgotten Realms had decades worth of metaplot, story arcs, character growth, etc. It was hard for new players to get into, but it was very popular with older players (who had been following all that for years or for more than a decade). When they went with 4th edition, they basically hit a big &quot;reset&quot; button on the Realms, throwing out all the metaplot, all the NPCs, introducing an entire new double-world, and killing/altering the relationships of a lot of gods. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately for them, the older players were pretty unhappy and weren't terribly interested in this &quot;new&quot; Forgotten Realms. And newer players weren't too interested because they were still intimidated by all of the old setting information. So 4th ed Forgotten Realms material wasn't selling well since the &quot;guaranteed&quot; market (the older fans who traditionally bought everything Forgotten Realms related) was generally unhappy, and new players still weren't buying it.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how this &quot;re-reset&quot; will affect things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T02:44:30-08:00","id":40427,"title":"","content":"I've dabbled in 2E and 4E, and played 3-3.5E pretty heavily. I used to think that I could tell whatever story I like regardless of the system I'm using. Now I realize that's bunk, and the Story <i>will</i> be shaped by the rules that govern it, even if that influence manifests in the ST having to rig up a bunch of house rules to support the type of story he and his players actually wanted.<br /> <br /> I find D&amp;D valuable, as a frequent GM/ST, because each edition tends to be very blatant about the different ways the system will shape the stories you'll use it to tell. Further, the stories the systems are geared to direct you towards tend to match the stories the fluff text in the books suggest. A lot of other systems are full of hidden dangers that result in the play experience being <i>very different</i> from the sort of stories the books, on the surface, seem to suggest. Anyone who tried to run a CWoD game using the rules strictly as written knows what I'm talking about. Every time I try another RPG system, or think about including a peripheral supplement to a system I already know, I have to spend time thinking about what those new rules will actually do when my players interact with them, and what kind of play those rules will encourage. That's rarely a problem with core D&amp;D stuff. It's a bit less certain with the enormous sprawl of peripherals that each edition accumulates, but having a well-defined foundation helps a lot when trying to figure out how those expansions will actually modify it.<br /> <br /> Is a game or two of D&amp;D worth the experience? Yes.<br /> Are you <i>less</i> of a &quot;true gamer&quot; if you don't ever get around to it? No.<br /> Are you <i>more</i> of a &quot;true gamer&quot; if you <i>shun</i> it? <i>Hell</i> no.<br /> <br /> Just remember the Mantra of Nerd Harmony - <i>It's OK for different people to like things that you dislike, and dislike things that you like. It's not OK to be an asshole about it, though.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T06:42:26-08:00","id":40490,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=40357#post40357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We'll see how that goes.<br /> <br /> They really shot themselves in the foot with the Spellplague. The Forgotten Realms had decades worth of metaplot, story arcs, character growth, etc. It was hard for new players to get into, but it was very popular with older players (who had been following all that for years or for more than a decade). When they went with 4th edition, they basically hit a big &quot;reset&quot; button on the Realms, throwing out all the metaplot, all the NPCs, introducing an entire new double-world, and killing/altering the relationships of a lot of gods.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately for them, the older players were pretty unhappy and weren't terribly interested in this &quot;new&quot; Forgotten Realms. And newer players weren't too interested because they were still intimidated by all of the old setting information. So 4th ed Forgotten Realms material wasn't selling well since the &quot;guaranteed&quot; market (the older fans who traditionally bought everything Forgotten Realms related) was generally unhappy, and new players still weren't buying it.<br /> <br /> I'm curious to see how this &quot;re-reset&quot; will affect things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with everything you posted.<br /> When I first discovered D&amp;D back in the 70s it was still pretty much new. And after Elric of Melnibone, Conan of Cimmeria, Fafhrd and Mouser, and so many others (other than Lord of the Rings), D&amp;D was so very open in terms of creating an atmosphere, the mood, look and feel of another world And it was kind of mind blowing back then. (Hearing how Snow White and the seven dwarves became Bahamut and his seven gold dragon minions was funny) But of the creation process was the idea of creating a refuge.<br /> When they began creating specific worlds, they began with Greyhawk and it was pretty awesome. The atmosphere was fairly gritty with the armies of Iuz running all over. But when they created the Forgotten realms...it was there that I feel there was that refuge. A character could go to the Dales and catch a breath and resupply. When they changed everything with 4e that was ruined. It was nice to see some additional ideas (such as primal casters) but the atmosphere was pretty much gone, along with a host of NPCs that the player was familiar with; The Knights of Myth Drannor, The Seven Sisters, the Zhentarim, Elminster and Khelben, Manshoon, etc....It seemed to me that they went from exploring one particular spot here and there, with the occasional event (Temple of Elemental Evil for example), to where your character would leap from one world crisis to another. (SpellPlague, the return of Netheril, the Abolethic Sovereignty, Neverwinter, etc...) It just seemed you couldn't catch a breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-01T09:21:17-08:00","id":40528,"title":"","content":"Nope. Never played it, either.<br /> <br /> I actually became interested in RPG's by watching Blade, which then made me interested in vampires, which then lead to me being interested in Vampire the Masquerade: Bloodlines, which then led me into the wonderful world of White Wolf.<br /> <br /> 11 years later, and I'm still hooked to this day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T18:01:22-07:00","id":97147,"title":"","content":"I hope people don't mind I'm bringing this thread back.<br /> <br /> My impression of DnD is, it is a RPG with training wheels (my experience is with versions 3.0/3.5 and a bit of pathfinder). It is difficult to make mistakes bad enough to wreck a character to the point of being unplayable (you would probably need to know what you are doing). The single most important choice you can make in the game is the character class you pick for your character. Your class determines nearly everything that your character can do, what special things it can do, what general things it can do well, and what things it does poorly at. Your character class is mostly set in stone. For instance, at level 5 all fighters have a +5 bonus to attack rolls because of their class, at that same level all wizards can get access to level 3 spells.<br /> <br /> Some classes are more sensitive to poor customization in other details (like ability scores such as strength) than other classes. A character with poor stats in strength, dexterity, and constitution probably shouldn't be a fighter; a wizard with poor stats in intelligence would be limited in the level of spells it can cast (or might be unable to cast spells at all). Other things might add to your abilities or improve performance of what you can do, but these are often things you can do without.<br /> <br /> The problem I have with such a system is it is difficult to break the mold. The classes are put together in ways that they are balanced with each other, but if you wanted to play something different than what was offered, it would be difficult to do the proper balance (the game didn't offer much support for that). Of course, moving to other game systems that are not class based but are point buy based, one comes to learn that it is easy to make broken characters. One would need some understanding of the rules, know what works and what doesn't work, and maybe played a few damaged characters to learn from experience, in order to make good characters. Example characters do help plenty, as does discussing what works for the game.<br /> <br /> Overall I prefer other games systems than DnD, even though they are simpler to set up a game for one (dungeon crawls are easy to setup).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/536-divinewrath","name":"DivineWrath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar536_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T18:21:17-07:00","id":97157,"title":"","content":"&gt;D&amp;D3.0/3.5<br /> &gt;balanced<br /> HA","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-23T20:52:28-07:00","id":97261,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't describe DnD as an RPG with training wheels.<br /> <br /> Well okay, roleplay wise, yes. It's not an immensely flexible thing(although more flexible than I think even the Wizards team realize), but once race and class are picked, there's a certain amount of railroading happening. On top of that, it plays with motifs and archetypes so engrained into the Western consciousness that it doesn't really take much explanation to get someone into their role (contrast that even with either Mages from WoD, where you'd think the idea of who and what you are would really be intrinsic but requires more education than you'd imagine). In terms of concept, it is very quick to pick up and play.<br /> <br /> But DnD-any edition-are all somewhere on the simulationist side of the roleplaying mechanics spectrum. There's a lot of information to memorize in order to run your game, and the nature of the math of the game is far from intuitive. Also, 4th Edition might have been the most dumbed down the game ever got, and it still quite often required multiple rolls to determine is something actually worked. Earlier editions were even more ridiculous in the nature of some of their demands. This frequently means that a DM either has to do frequent heavy lifting or fudgery, or a player has to read the book just to get an idea of how they can do anything. Contrast this, again, with at least WoD, which while not ridiculously easy to understand is still fairly quick to pick up and understand and execute, with players needing to read to understand the depths of what they can do.<br /> <br /> Yeah, DnD is a beginner game in some ways, but not enough so that I feel I could ever describe it as having training wheels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T11:11:30-07:00","id":97622,"title":"","content":"I suspect that the original game was awesome compared to what it became with 4e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T14:34:54-07:00","id":97754,"title":"","content":"You would be wrong sir. I have a brother who kept editions of Advanced 2nd Edition and prior, and I was into 3rd, 3.5, and 4th Editions.<br /> <br /> 3rd, 3.5, and 4th have cleaned up a metric shit ton of the problems found in the earlier editions(although that's a matter of perspective, although the main counter I can think of it is my crotchety and unreliable brother), and each had their pros and cons compared to each other-4th was easier to get people to play and the most streamlined of the editions, 3rd was more expansive and flexible if unnessecarily weighty-but the assessment I gave before this more or less holds true-conceptually it's easy to grasp what you, the heroes, are supposed to do, but mechanically(even 4e, which is very DnD for Dummies, for better or for worse) it's always been very heavy mechanically.<br /> <br /> But Chainmail and the original DnD, and even the ADnD set were really just godawful. I excuse it purely on the grounds that they were pioneering an entirely new thing, but it was just an incredibly jumbled mess. If you want to contend that ADnD 2nd Edition were better than 4th, I've seen enough charm to that system to maybe give you the benefit of perspective, but the first three (two if you don't count the original Chainmail run) clearly make 4th Edition look good in comparison. At least 4th was consistent and clear with itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T16:26:57-07:00","id":97844,"title":"","content":"That's just it. I think it was that inconsistency, that chaos and utter mess, that encouraged the imagination. Kinda like a fine piece of abstract art of a scene versus a digitized model of the same scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T17:53:30-07:00","id":97925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowflame</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=97844#post97844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's just it. I think it was that inconsistency, that chaos and utter mess, that encouraged the imagination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait wait wait.... So, you'd be more happy with a book that was filled with typos because that would encourage your imagination than you would be with one that was 100% technically correct? Not referring to D&amp;D here, but just books in general.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For these reasons, the trade of a soldier is held the most honourable of all others; because a soldier is a Yahoo hired to kill, in cold blood, as many of his own species, who have never offended him, as possibly he can.&quot; \u2015 from &quot;Gulliver's Travels&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1041-brjedi26","name":"brjedi26","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1041_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"495"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T18:35:53-07:00","id":97962,"title":"","content":"I don't want to detract from Br's question, because it's a good one, but three things:<br /> <br /> 1) I like a certain chaos sometimes. This wasn't chaos. This was picking through the scrapyard to find two things that fit together in such away that made 3rd/3.5 seem sane. If 3rd Edition was arcane in it's minutiae and ADnD 2 arcane in it's presentation, then earlier editions were a confusing mesh of arcane academia speak and bits of lopsided lucidity arranged awkwardly by the wizards apprentice after. It was a poor grimoire, the early editions.<br /> 2) Look, I know I've read them. Maybe you should read them before assuming the chaos helps.<br /> <br /> 3) Revenge of the TV Head put forth an idea that kind of sums up all of my experience with DnD in general, from the awkward few games with my oldest brother to the fumblings of 3rd and the tediousness of 4th-I had fun with DnD in spite of the game, not because of the game.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, you gotta understand that the best games of DnD I had <i>were with 4th Edition</i>. Not because the game, by itself, was good, but because it was the closest DnD ever got to shutting up and getting out of the way with its' mechanics. Limited, narrow mechanics it might have been, but it also didn't take forever to just understand how to resolve stuff-it was about as close to roll and move on as DnD got with a majority of its' rules.<br /> <br /> 4th Edition wasn't a bad game(if we're using DnD in general as a standard, move away from that, and the entire game regardless of edition clearly shows signs of entropy), it was a <i>different</i> game, with some radically new design direction that, while used in RPG's before(seriously, there are games that use a lot of the conceits from 4th Edition that actually work and are likable), hadn't been quite displayed that way before and didn't have to contend with a DnD legacy. WHile the translation isn't clean, it's rather like how Mummy and Promethean are rather different games for World of Darkness-within the context, neither of those games are really bad(in fact I love them both and in fact that in terms of idea, Promethean might be perfect, although the mechanics don't quite match up.), but they don't do as well because the ideas at work are, well, very different from the rest.<br /> <br /> 4th Edition has the same problem, it just showcases more because of how much it stood out both mechanically and 'fluffily' compared to its' elder brothers. Does it have problems? yes, I am the first to say that. But I think it has less problems than people think it does, because so much of it was the radical change of idea from all the earlier editions. And to be fair, so much of what was done was done in response to a large number of problems DnD has always had and which, now that we have 4th Edition looking all problematic on the side, are almost actively ignored by the fans of the game now. There were shitstorms aplenty for both 3rd and 3.5 editions, and yet now so many people treat those games like the Holy Grail of DnD because it's not 4th.<br /> <br /> So, to recap point three: Yes, I think 4th Edition was a flawed idea and execution. No, I don't think it's the worst DnD has ever put out, just very, very different, and as such will work better with less traditional groups of DnD. No, I don't think 4th is worse that Chainmail, DnD, or ADnD. Maybe, it might be worse than ADnD 2, and Yes, despite all of that, I had not one, but two really awesome games with 4th Edition, where as I can only claim mediocrity with all the others.<br /> <br /> And Yes-ish, I don't think DnD on the whole is actually a good game anymore, regardless of edition. It's certainly not the worst, it may not even really be bad, but it's definitely not good.<br /> <br /> Simply put, my experience with the game does not line up with what everyone else is saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T08:40:59-07:00","id":98384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With this in mind, you gotta understand that the best games of DnD I had <i>were with 4th Edition</i>. Not because the game, by itself, was good, but because it was the closest DnD ever got to shutting up and getting out of the way with its' mechanics. Limited, narrow mechanics it might have been, but it also didn't take forever to just understand how to resolve stuff-it was about as close to roll and move on as DnD got with a majority of its' rules. </div> </div> </div>Either we haven't been playing the same D&amp;D's or you really aren't someone who can grasp the 'crunchy'-aspects of RPG if you think D&amp;D's system to be over-complex compared to its contemporaries in any way or form. Adding your skill bonus to a roll of d20 to pass a set target number truly doesn't equal some higher understanding of algebra in 3.x or just rolling below your attribute in early D&amp;D's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T08:48:46-07:00","id":98388,"title":"","content":"3rd/3.5 Editions base mechanic is very simple, yes. I'm thinking things like grappling, attacks of opportunity, some of the aspects of magic, etc., etc(and there were a <i>lot</i> of these subsystems all over the place). Granted, the math is also a little more obnoxious compared to a lot of other game systems(and I own quite a lot, as I mentioned in the Non-WW RPG thread), and thus more annoying than I like, but it's not bad in and of itself.<br /> <br /> DnD is just always very unwieldy and very in the way. 4th Edition did a lot to minimize that, at the cost of a lot of the wonderful flexibility and creativity of earlier editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T13:38:17-07:00","id":98619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>brjedi26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait wait wait.... So, you'd be more happy with a book that was filled with typos because that would encourage your imagination than you would be with one that was 100% technically correct? Not referring to D&amp;D here, but just books in general.</div> </div> </div> </div> You misunderstand the timeframe. There wasn't anything like it at the time. It was originally set for medieval and yes, Tolkien's material, and it encouraged a desire for more. And when they finally hit us with that 1st edition, it still made you want more. Those first images in those books were iconic. Such as: <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://www.tor.com/images/stories/blogs/11_09/saladinahmed/trampier%20-%20emirikol.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T15:47:10-07:00","id":98722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=98388#post98388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3rd/3.5 Editions base mechanic is very simple, yes. I'm thinking things like grappling, attacks of opportunity, some of the aspects of magic, etc., etc(and there were a <i>lot</i> of these subsystems all over the place). Granted, the math is also a little more obnoxious compared to a lot of other game systems(and I own quite a lot, as I mentioned in the Non-WW RPG thread), and thus more annoying than I like, but it's not bad in and of itself.<br /> <br /> DnD is just always very unwieldy and very in the way. 4th Edition did a lot to minimize that, at the cost of a lot of the wonderful flexibility and creativity of earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>First off; My apologies for being perhaps overly confrontational but I get agitated when someone claims 4th ed of d&amp;d better D&amp;D than the previous editions because its anything but imo.<br /> <br /> The biggest reason for me to hate 4th is its disregard to levelling system which in the old D&amp;D was the basic unit to measure characters overall power inside its class.<br /> Sure, in current trend of RPG's levels are considered archaich but to me they're very D&amp;D. Honestly whats the point of Tiers if all they do is double your Hp and the damage you do and double the Hp &amp; damage of monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:12:24-07:00","id":98744,"title":"","content":"The sum point for me is that I think that 4th isn't nessecarily better or worse than 3/.5, it was just a different experience....backed up by a weird sort of love/hate relationship with DnD on the whole. When I get right down to it, I like DnD from ADnD 2 to 4th(3rd to 4th better than ADnD 2, but I still like the outlier well enough), but when I honestly appraise DnD, I find a game that I can't bring myself to call good. It's not <i>bad-</i>well, actually, it might be, but it's a tolerable and semi-endearing bad if it is. But I know I can't call it good, not in my opinion. 4th Edition tried to fix a lot of things and take the game in a new direction for a new era, and in some ways that I like, it worked....but it still tripped over itself in some big ways. At the end of the day, I've had good experiences with both systems, and yet objectively looking at both I still kind of go &quot;How the hell did I do that?&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's a game I think everyone in RPG's should play, with 3rd(Well, fuck am I kidding, 3.5, it's harder to get the range of support for 3rd) or 4th Edition being chosen more for differing play style based on the group(people who don't mind the tediousness of one for the greater flexibility, and one where the system might be limiting but also moves along faster so you can get back to other things faster...or back to the same thing if it's cool wit y'all)...but I don't think I would ever actively seek to play a game of DnD myself again.<br /> <br /> Which seems bizarre, because I'm still planning on buying DnD Next/5th Edition/THe Next Generation/FuckADoodleDoo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:18:05-07:00","id":98751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which seems bizarre, because I'm still planning on buying DnD Next/5th Edition/THe Next Generation/FuckADoodleDoo.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yep! Me too. And I don't even play games. Which makes me seem even more bizarre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:53:30-07:00","id":98771,"title":"","content":"...Like, not even WoD, new or old?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:58:02-07:00","id":98778,"title":"","content":"I might buy 5th ed to complete my D&amp;D collection but I doubt I'll be interested in playing or running it except as a one shot to test the system in practise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1700-blue-fox","name":"Blue Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T05:55:21-07:00","id":99087,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=98771#post98771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Like, not even WoD, new or old?</div> </div> </div> </div>Too solitary...don't play well with others, you know the drill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Mankind was once an endangered species. It will likely be so again. And mankind will only have itself to blame.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/144-shadowflame","name":"Shadowflame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T10:18:20-07:00","id":99269,"title":"","content":"Never readf or played anything DnD. I'm not sure I would really enjoy the whole dungeon crawl thing. I have played tons of non-WW games, from Witchcraft to Deadlands to Cthulhu, just not DnD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/961-chewygranola","name":"ChewyGranola","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"254"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T18:07:54-07:00","id":99623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ChewyGranola</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=99269#post99269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never readf or played anything DnD. I'm not sure I would really enjoy the whole dungeon crawl thing. I have played tons of non-WW games, from Witchcraft to Deadlands to Cthulhu, just not DnD.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting thing to note: D&amp;D doesn't have to be a dungeon crawl, that's just something it does which most other games don't try to do - you can actually play D&amp;D just like Deadlands, or even like Call of Cthulhu if your players are the sort that always find a way to get magical powers while investigating. I do both frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:16:10-07:00","id":99648,"title":"","content":"I started my gaming with Vampire the Requiem, and the very next day, Exalted 1st Edition. It wasn't until... about two years ago that I ever picked up or read a DnD book. In fact, because I was so into White-Wolf, I actively avoided it... for some reason, me and my group felt it would corrupt our 'pure' storytelling experience to dirty ourselves with DnD.<br /> <br /> Of course, once we actually sank our teeth in to it, it was actually pretty fun. About a year later, I threw down quite a bit of money on the Pathfinder books, and we've played it often enough. Not as fun as any of White-Wolf's material, of course, but it has its own flavor.<br /> <br /> Still, I started off without DnD, and am oddly proud of the fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T19:17:27-07:00","id":99649,"title":"","content":"I can only think of two crawls outside of very short experiments. The experiments weren't very good(I blame the runner of said experiments), and of the two that took place in main games-no, it was three, One was bad, one was celerly shortened by the players, and one was aight.<br /> <br /> Most of our time was not spent in a traditional dungeon crawl, but rather a general pattern of setup and fallout born from the machinations of personal issues and organizational conflicts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-26-2014, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T07:01:24-07:00","id":99981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/32023-am-i-the-only-rpg-nerd-that-never-read-a-dnd-book?p=99648#post99648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I started my gaming with Vampire the Requiem, and the very next day, Exalted 1st Edition. It wasn't until... about two years ago that I ever picked up or read a DnD book. In fact, because I was so into White-Wolf, I actively avoided it... for some reason, me and my group felt it would corrupt our 'pure' storytelling experience to dirty ourselves with DnD.<br /> <br /> Of course, once we actually sank our teeth in to it, it was actually pretty fun. About a year later, I threw down quite a bit of money on the Pathfinder books, and we've played it often enough. Not as fun as any of White-Wolf's material, of course, but it has its own flavor.<br /> <br /> Still, I started off without DnD, and am oddly proud of the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good for you for being open to new experiences.<br /> <br /> Pathfinder is the version of D&amp;D I play most at the moment. It is where I get my fantasy adventure fix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I game. This is the way.</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8-storyteller","name":"Storyteller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-28T18:38:13-07:00","id":101019,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Keep it civil people. If you don't like a post that doesn't give you permission to attack the person making the post, this is the only warning being given as you should all know this by now.</span></b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-31T14:55:04-07:00","id":102948,"title":"","content":"I started with DnD, but played mostly White-Wolf stuff in the late 90's early 2000's.<br /> I find DnD to be good for my Tolkien fantasy fix. I hardly think you need DnD to be a &quot;real&quot; RPG nerd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/767-lostinsanity","name":"LostInSanity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-05T15:17:48-07:00","id":106554,"title":"","content":"Actually, I started out playing Palladium's Robotech; then we got into AD&amp;D and Battletech. If you like the Tolkenesque fantasy genre in which you go on adventures, slay monsters and get lots of treasure, fame with out a lot of social RPG situations etc, then D&amp;D is right for you. If you like more RPG while still being somewhat powerful, WW is the pay forward. <br /> <br /> Since I have read more history books than fantasy, I prefer a bit more RPGing, but I do like fantasy. The one thing I do not like about the Fantasy-genre, is the vast open country-side with no people. Historically, even, &quot;Wilderness&quot;, will have people and every mile or so, expect a village with farmers and every one-hundred miles, expect a chief/lord and every 1,000 miles, expect a king.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T16:54:29-07:00","id":107778,"title":"","content":"That has precisely fuck all to do with the Genre and entirely upon the kind of GM you're playing with.<br /> <br /> <br /> And a vast countryside with no people is perfectly sensible if the local fauna is malicious, sentient and man eating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T19:17:23-07:00","id":107882,"title":"","content":"I was roped into a DnD game once, but the game disbanded after a practice session (to understand the mechanics), and a couple proper sessions. I never really read the book as much as I asked my friend running the thing to help me build a character and I learned as I played the game.<br /> <br /> I am certain the game we played was 4th Edition.<br /> <br /> I started playing Vampire: the Masquerade (the Dark Ages line to start, actually) after enjoying the computer game Bloodlines. I then played Revised, bought V20 when that came out, ran a few games in turn with friends, and messed around with the New World of Darkness. I don't have much experience with DnD at all - most of my experiences are in homebrew games, Vampire, and Star Wars SAGA. I have been asked to go to a couple LARP games, but the games I have played really don't interest me that much (probably due to being too lazy to swing a foam hammer).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1592-jack","name":"Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1592_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T05:23:13-07:00","id":108119,"title":"","content":"I began my career with D&amp;D, like many gamers. I played it for a while, but some years ago I realized that 3e is just terrible and the other editions aren't for me. I've moved on to the White Wolf games by now, although I'd very much like to try GURPS. The general type of game D&amp;D represents suits me, but the rules are just inexcusable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/186-morty","name":"Morty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar186_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}